course: dictionary
lesson: 1686
title: Christmas, a proper noun
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A proper noun is the name of one special person, place or thing, so it always starts with a capital letter. Christmas is a proper noun, so write Christmas, never christmas. Its plural is Christmases.
explain: Christmas has two meanings. First, it is the Christian festival in December that celebrates the birth of Jesus. Second, it is the whole holiday season around it, with presents, decorations and family meals. Read the words around it to see which meaning is used.
explain: The last verse asks: «Who were the first to cry Nowell? / Animals all, as it befell». Nowell is another name for Noel, a shout of joy at Christmas, and befell means happened. Old words like these have clues too: the rest of the verse shows you what they mean.
explain: Words change from place to place. «Merry Christmas» became «Mele Kalikimaka» in Hawaiian, because Hawaiian has no r, s or t, and its syllables end in vowels. Some people say "happy holidays" instead, so that everyone feels included.
fact: Christmas is a proper noun, so it always starts with a capital C.
fact: Christmas means the Christian festival in December that celebrates the birth of Jesus.
fact: Christmas can also mean the holiday season around it, with presents, decorations and family meals.
fact: Christmases is the plural, and it is also written with a capital C.
fact: «Freddie in England has a cold Christmas, but his cousin in Australia is at the beach in his togs (swimming costume).» Christmas is in summer there, because the seasons are the other way round in the southern half of the world.
exercise: Which spelling is correct for the festival? | christmas | christMas | *Christmas | Christmass
exercise: In «Who were the first to cry Nowell? Animals all, as it befell», what does befell mean? | Ran away | Hid | *Happened | Sang
exercise: Freddie's cousin in Australia is at the beach at Christmas. Why? | Christmas is in winter there | Togs are needed for winter | *Christmas is in summer there | The beach is closed in December
test: «We put up the decorations for Christmas.» Here Christmas means | A kind of swimming costume | A school test | *The holiday season, with decorations and presents | A month of winter in France
test: Which line has the correct capital letters? | merry christmas | Merry christmas | merry Christmas | *Merry Christmas
exam: What is a proper noun? | A word for an action | A word that joins two sentences | *A name for one special person, place or thing, always with a capital letter | A word that describes a feeling
